<p style=3D"line-height:1.2"><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;"><strong>Date:=
</strong> Wednesday, August 26<sup>th</sup><span style=3D"white-space-colla=
pse: preserve;"> </span><strong>Time:</strong> 10:00 AM PT / 1:00 PM ET</sp=
an></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:100%; font-size:14px">&nbsp;</p>
<p style=3D"line-height:1.2"><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">You will lear=
n:</span></p>
<ul style=3D"line-height:175%">
<li><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">Why text-based retrieval creates redun=
dant context</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">Where connected evidence delivers the =
greatest gains</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">How graph traversals become concise ev=
idence packages</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">Why retrieval architecture improves ef=
ficiency and accuracy</span></li>
<li><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">When GraphRAG or Vector RAG is the rig=
ht choice</span></li>
</ul>
<p style=3D"line-height:1.2"><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">This is not a=
nother theoretical comparison of retrieval technologies. It is a practical =
look at what hundreds of real GraphRAG applications revealed.</span></p>
<p style=3D"line-height:1.2"><span style=3D"font-size: 14px;">Join us tomor=
row.</span></p>
